ll, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Now I'll add a regression test and run it.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, and Python's built-in `round()` works on that stored value. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. The function's docstring promises \"half up\", but it never did that.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): the function now rounds the shortest decimal form of the number (`repr(x)`, i.e. `\"2.675\"`) with `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`. It still returns a float. `add_vat` uses it, so VAT amounts get the same rounding.\n\n**Check:** I ran the cases directly with `python3`:\n- `2.675 \u2192 2.68`\n- `1.005 \u2192 1.01`\n- `0.125 \u2192 0.13`\n- `2.674 \u2192 2.67`\n- `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68` (halves round away from zero)\n- `3 \u2192 3.0`\n- `split(10.00, 3)` is unchanged at `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`\n\nI added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases, but haven't run it: pytest isn't installed here, so neither it nor the existing `tests/test_split.py` was run under pytest.\n\n**Limit:** this fixes prices that come in as written. A value that floating-point arithmetic has already pushed just below the half (for example a product that comes out as `2.6749999992`) still rounds down. The only full fix for that is to keep amounts as `Decimal` throughout.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 239405, "requests_cache_write": 18645, "requests_cost_usd": 0.184466, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2164, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 